# --- Line endings ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# LF in the repository AND in the working copy, on every platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a per-machine setting, so without this file the working
# copy's line endings depend on who cloned it. That matters more here than in
# most repos: #30 makes a file watcher the integration surface between the app
# and the agent, and two processes writing the same file (#31) must not disagree
# about what a line ending is. A CRLF/LF flip rewrites every line of a file —
# which reads as "everything changed" to a watcher, a diff, and the change
# feed (#16) alike.
#
# It also keeps the handoff package honest (#19): docs/plan/ is committed into
# someone else's repo, and it should not arrive with this machine's line
# endings baked in.

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Windows-native scripts ------------------------------------------------
#
# The one real exception. Batch files are interpreted by cmd.exe, which has
# historically mis-parsed LF-only files. PowerShell handles LF fine, so .ps1
# stays with everything else above.

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# --- Binary ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Git detects most of these, but declaring them means no chance of a text
# heuristic mangling one. references/media/ is ten infographics (#0 source
# material) and must never be touched.

*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# --- Diff hints ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nicer hunk headers when these start existing.

*.md   diff=markdown
*.ts   diff=typescript
*.tsx  diff=typescript
*.js   diff=javascript
*.jsx  diff=javascript
